          Lecture 3 of 5 in AI-Native Agent Security & Compliance.<br />
Lecture 1: risk moves from bad text to bad actions.<br />
Lecture 2: walls live in the harness, sandbox, and human-in-the-loop.<br />
Lecture 3: <strong>least privilege on real products. Before each tool call, the system must make a bounded decision: allow, deny, or escalate.</strong>
        </p>

        <p>
          Formula: <strong>Agent = Model + Harness + Tools + Permissions + Data</strong>. This session focuses on <strong>Permissions</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Guest <strong>Zachry Xiong</strong>, 15 minutes on Jev (TypeSafe AI, Sep 2026): state plus typed questions in; choice, score, or yes/no with probabilities out. Use it as a tool gate. It does not replace a sandbox or human review. <strong>Type safety is not correctness. Confidence is not authorization.</strong>
        </p>

